title The card named its Git nib in nine characters, one short of resolving
prompt Continue the overnight incense loop per recursion-prompts/incense-inner.md and the baton's rite: round-open, claim, cold run, pick an agent-doable finding, build it, send, log.
think Round-open opened clean at HEAD 85b014179, no standing rebase.
think Claim board read clear -- five live claims, none overlapping tools/ or construction/ at the path level.
think Launched the cold run; a live, non-stale pass already held the roster lock at the same settled HEAD (confirmed via tools/f/fleet_call.sh, verdict=dry, this tree's own). Waited for it rather than TERMing it, per the FLEET clause and the eighth-firing lesson on this baton.
think Cold run closed tree_moved=no, run_verdict=guard_red, 378 guards: 344 green, 31 red, 3 gated.
think Read nib_honesty's evidence: the scan reported git_nib_lines=0, git_nib=absent, verdict=NO_NIB_FIELD -- yet construction/ITINERARY.md plainly names a Git nib at line 353.
think The scan's classify_tokens function requires an exact ten-hex-character run to recognize any token at all (the tree's own git rev-parse --short=10 convention). The card's Git nib field read `e131f90ed` -- nine characters -- so the ten-char pattern never matched the token and the field became invisible to the classifier entirely, rather than merely misclassified.
think Confirmed with git rev-parse --short=10 e131f90ed that the correct ten-character form is e131f90ede, and confirmed e131f90ed is still HEAD's parent (git log --oneline -3), so the fix is a one-character correction rather than a nib refresh.
think A grep for the bare nine-char form elsewhere found only two dated citations (incense-inner.md's own next-log prose and a session log naming a landed commit) -- ordinary git short-hash citations rather than the Git-nib field this guard reads, and testimony under accrete-never-break, so neither needed touching.
obs Booked no REDS row: the ledger reads 268 bytes of headroom against its 65,536-byte bound, pin_deadlocked=1, zero foldable rows -- unchanged from every recent lap's reading. Recorded the mechanism in this log and the commit body instead.
file construction/ITINERARY.md -- corrected the Git nib field from a nine-character hash to its proper ten-character short form, e131f90ed to e131f90ede, so tools/n/nib_honesty_witness.rish's token classifier can see the field at all.
loom witness=nib_honesty_witness verdict=green guards_run=378 guards_green=344 guards_red_before=31 guards_red_after=30
rota lap 5140, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears. Read for what a guard's silence on a field it cannot even see says, rather than what it says when it sees one wrong: git_nib_lines=0 read as absence rather than as malformed, and the card had been saying its nib the whole time in a voice one character short of the shape the guard listens for.
scope construction/ITINERARY.md, recursion-prompts/incense-inner.md, this shelf and its index row
status GREEN -- nib_honesty_witness.rish re-run on metal, both remotes pushed at d39b38b62
recommend kg -- witness GREEN on metal, one-file one-line change, ready to send.
